  "visible_text": "VOLUME PACKING / POLYCUBE PARCEL\n\nFill the parcel without a hidden gap.\n\nOrbit the 3D parcel, select and rotate every rigid polycube about its axes, then drag each piece into the lattice. Inspect the back and fill all 27 cells exactly once with no overlap. Use only screenshots and visible controls in the task webpage. Do not use code, scripts, automation, Developer Tools, console, debugger, inspector, network, source, DOM or page-state inspection, terminal, shell, Python, address-bar or URL/query edits, reload or navigation, browser extensions, external applications, hidden state, or unrelated tabs.\n\nOCCUPIED CELLS\n27\n/ 27 \u00b7 7 / 7 pieces\nDIRECT CAMERA / PIECE DRAG\nYAW 98\u00b0 \u00b7 PITCH 33\u00b0\nV\nL\nT\nZ\nA\nB\nP\nRotate the view to inspect the back. The gold wire parcel is a volume, not a flat outline.\n\nSUPPLIED PIECES\n\nV\nV-CUT\nIN PARCEL\nL\nL-BEND\nIN PARCEL\nT\nT-BRACE\nIN PARCEL\nZ\nZIG\nIN PARCEL\nA\nLEFT ARM\nIN PARCEL\nB\nRIGHT ARM\nIN PARCEL\nP\nHOOK\nIN PARCEL\n\nSELECTED PIECE\n\nChoose a loose polycube.\nX \u221290\u00b0\nX +90\u00b0\nY \u221290\u00b0\nY +90\u00b0\nZ \u221290\u00b0\nZ +90\u00b0\n\nTurn the selected rigid piece about a world axis.\n\nCAMERA\n\nDrag an empty part of the scene to orbit around the parcel.\n\nCANCEL SELECTION\nABANDON ATTEMPT\nCERTIFY PARCEL\nPASS"
